---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro";
---

<Legal
  noindex
  title="Support — Saverr"
  description="Support for Saverr (com.propertysaver.app): where your data lives, backups, common questions and how to get in touch."
>
  <p class="app">Saverr</p>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p class="dates">For the Saverr app (com.propertysaver.app)</p>

  <nav class="pagetabs" aria-label="Saverr pages">
    <a href="/saverr/privacy">Privacy</a>
    <a href="/saverr/support" aria-current="page">Support</a>
  </nav>

  <p class="lede">
    Something not working, or a question the app doesn&rsquo;t answer? The
    questions below cover most of it — if not, get in touch.
  </p>

  <div class="contact">
    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Tell me what happened and I&rsquo;ll get back to you. For bugs, it helps
      to include your device, your OS version, the app version, and what you did
      just before it went wrong.
    </p>
    <p class="contact-line">
      <strong>B Xu</strong><br />
      <a href="mailto:bxu1.developer@gmail.com">bxu1.developer@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Common questions</h2>

    <details>
      <summary>Where is my data stored?</summary>
      <p>
        On your device, in the app&rsquo;s private storage. Saverr has no
        account and no server, so your shortlist and notes are never uploaded
        anywhere.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How do I back up my shortlist?</summary>
      <p>
        Use the backup screen to export your shortlist as a JSON file, then
        choose where it goes — Files, email, a cloud drive. Keep it somewhere
        you trust: it contains your listings, details and notes.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How do I delete a listing?</summary>
      <p>
        Open the listing and use the bin icon in the top right. The listing and
        its notes are removed from your device.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What happens when I tap &ldquo;Open listing&rdquo;?</summary>
      <p>
        The link is handed to your browser, which opens the original listing
        site. That site&rsquo;s own terms and privacy policy apply from there.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Does Saverr need an internet connection?</summary>
      <p>
        No. The app works offline. The only time it leaves your device is when
        you open a listing in your browser, or export a backup.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Is there an account, or a way to sync between devices?</summary>
      <p>
        There is no account, and no sync — everything stays on the device it was
        entered on. To move a shortlist, export a backup file and take it with
        you.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <p class="note">
    Saverr is made by Bill Xu. What the app stores, and why, is covered in the <a href="/saverr/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
